  "text": "Prompt engineering enables end users of an llm to customize the output of the LLM by stating in the prompt how the LLM should respond. It relies on existing pattern recognition ability of the LLM and does not add, change, or act on parameters of an LLM. Examples in the prompt acts_as training examples. Zero shot prompting supplies examples in the prompt with none, but might give information about the technology company apple instead of the fruit when the zero shot prompt that mentions only the word apple is used. An llm benefits from context. Few shot prompting gives multiple examples in the prompt and can show that a plum is a drupe or that a pear is a pome, while asking for the fruit family of a lemon. One shot prompting gives one example in the prompt and can show that a peach belongs to the drupe fruit family or ask for the fruit family of an apple.",
  "reason": "The text synthesizes all supplied relations into a single coherent narrative. It begins with 'prompt engineering' enabling users, noting its reliance on pattern recognition and lack of parameter modification. It then describes 'examples in the prompt' acting as training data, followed by specific prompting strategies: 'zero shot' supplying examples (with potential ambiguity about company vs. fruit info), 'few shot' providing multiple examples and demonstrating specific fruit facts (plum, pear) while querying others (lemon), and 'one shot' providing a single example and demonstrating other fruit facts (peach, apple). The order follows the source occurrence in the supplied relations list."
